## Logs

The dev terminal prints one line per request and one `chat request` line per reply with model, tokens, and cost. `bun run dev` also keeps two files in `logs/`: `dev.log` is a plain-text copy of the terminal, including Vite and render errors, and `server.jsonl` has the app's logs as JSON lines for scripts and agents. API responses carry an `x-request-id` header that matches the `requestId` on its log lines. Starting `bun run dev` moves the previous run's files to `logs/*.prev.*`. In production, logs are JSON lines on stdout and no files are written.

