## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `bun install` | Install dependencies and git hooks |
| `bun run dev` | Dev server; also writes `logs/dev.log` and `logs/server.jsonl` |
| `bun run dev:bg` / `bun run dev:stop` | The same dev server in the background (for agents and scripts): reuses one that's already running, returns once it's up |
| `bun run lint` | Biome lint and format check |
| `bun run typecheck` | Route typegen + tsc |
| `bun run check` | The full gate: lint, typecheck, test, and e2e (which builds first) |
| `bun run test` | Tests (no network) |
| `bun run test:watch` | Tests in watch mode |
| `bun run coverage` | Tests with coverage |
| `bun run e2e` | Browser smoke test: the production build in Chromium against a stub OpenRouter |
| `bun run build` | Production build |
| `bun run start` | Serve the production build |
| `bun run format` | Apply Biome formatting and safe fixes |
| `bun run clean` | Remove build output, caches, and logs |

Use `bun run test`, not `bun test`: the tests run on vitest, and `bun test` is bun's own runner. `bun run` with no arguments lists every script.

## Working in this repo

- `AGENTS.md` is the map: architecture, conventions, and where things go. Coding agents read it first; it's the fastest orientation for people too.
- The chat (`app/routes/chat.tsx` → `api.chat.ts` → `app/.server/chat.ts`) is the reference path through the stack. `/extract` is the smallest complete feature slice to copy when adding one.
- The chat export (`app/.server/export.ts`, `app/routes/api.chats.$chatId.export.ts`, `tests/chat-export.test.ts`) is the smallest GET resource route with a path param, to copy for read-only endpoints.
- In Claude Code: `/add-route` adds a feature slice end to end, `/check` runs the gate and fixes failures, and the `reviewer` agent reviews a change before you commit. Hooks hand the agent type errors (and lint errors, with the agent-ops hooks) right after each edit and point it at a dev server you already have running, so it reads the same `logs/` you do. `.claude/README.md` lists them all.
- VS Code: open the folder and accept the recommended extensions. The Run and Debug panel has "Debug dev server" and "Debug current test file".

